flowchart TB
  accTitle: How a visit's score counts
  accDescr: A score its darts can't make, such as 179, is refused. What is left checks out where the darts can finish it and busts where they can't, such as 159 with double out. More than is left busts, such as 100 from 32, as does 1 left with double out. Any other score leaves the rest. After a bust or the rest, the next player throws.
  SCORE["A visit's score"] --> MADE{"Can its darts<br/>make it?"}
  MADE -- "no, such as 179" --> REFUSED["Refused:<br/>check the score"]
  MADE -- "yes" --> LEFT{"Exactly what<br/>is left?"}
  LEFT -- "yes" --> FINISH{"Can the darts<br/>finish it?"}
  FINISH -- "yes" --> CHECKOUT["Checkout:<br/>the leg is won"]
  FINISH -- "no, such as 159<br/>with double out" --> BUST["Bust: the score<br/>stays as it was"]
  LEFT -- "no" --> MORE{"More, or 1 left<br/>with double out?"}
  MORE -- "yes, such as<br/>100 from 32" --> BUST
  MORE -- "no" --> REST["It leaves the rest"]
  BUST --> NEXT["The next player throws"]
  REST --> NEXT
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef warn fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
  class CHECKOUT,REST done
  class BUST,REFUSED warn
